  "findings": [
    "The selector-6 command carrier is 434.461993 MHz, matching the retained enrollment routine carrier rather than the earlier selector-5 command channel.",
    "Five minutes is encoded as 0x0096 two-second units and fifteen minutes as 0x01c2; the on-air little-endian fields are 96 00 and c2 01.",
    "Combined with earlier commands whose low-byte bit 7 was originally clear, these captures preserve the HTV145 rule that bit 7 is overlaid with OR rather than added to the two-byte count.",
    "The selector-6 association reverses the high marker bit on request/response family byte 1: open is 90/d0 and close is 10/50. The stable semantic discriminators are request body byte 2 (82 open, 81 close) and response usage-marker byte 5 (cf watering, 4f idle).",
    "The command sequence is not a simple increment per cloud API call: the first close and second open both used sequence 82. Counter synchronization must continue to use authenticated observed traffic, not API-call count."
  ]
